# Prospective decision: preserve kernel process proof after resolver self-proc refusal

Status: SOURCE DESIGN ONLY / NOT ADMISSION. This records a bounded local control-plane proof design. It neither changes ADR-0040's Proposed/adoption status nor authorizes runtime, source activation or protected publication. Frozen caller07/resolver02, consumed dfe68/63d164 authority, UNKNOWN result8efd/entrydff9, old keeperce9a and its stopped state remain historical. No restart, reuse of consumed permit, writable /tmp, extra RW mount, SDK/SQL, source editing or automatic retry.

## Evidence and hypothesis

Actual Node24.20.0 exited1 opening /proc/self/stat via binding.readFileUtf8, with EROFS/open and no stdout. It failed before the loader/graph/root collection. The caller's earlier external PID1 reads are not a successful Node-self proof. Owned stop exited0/stderr0 and final sameCID Runningfalse; retain actual final Exit137 and deprecation stdout without inferring TERM-only cleanup. Inspector whole failure scope20e081 is CLOSED.

Primary QEMU source synthesizes self stat/cmdline, recognizes both self and decimal getpid paths, virtualizes self-exe, and tries memfd before an ENOSYS temporary-file fallback. Current source also realpaths proc paths. These are relevant mechanisms, not an exact-build identification of kernel executable9376 or a syscall trace from this failure. EROFS is consistent with a temporary-file fallback under rootRO, but that causal explanation remains unproven. The Node fs source uses read defaults. Buffer reads, a decimal path or an FD alias cannot be assumed to cure either the error or the virtualized-exe identity. No write was requested by the workspace resolver source.

Primary references: [QEMU v7.2 syscall implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qemu/qemu/v7.2.0/linux-user/syscall.c) functions is_proc_myself/do_openat/readlink handling; [current QEMU syscall implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qemu/qemu/master/linux-user/syscall.c) maybe_do_fake_open; [Node24.20 fs source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/node/v24.20.0/lib/fs.js) readFileSync default flag. These are source explanations, not exact installed QEMU provenance or a complete runtime fs.js byte match. The preliminary statement that v7.2 always uses mkstemp was incorrect; both reviewed versions try memfd first.

