## Strong reserve: external live-process rendezvous

If numeric self access cannot satisfy the actual kernel fence, use a distinct reviewed `populated-history-target-linux-resolution-03/resolve_target_linux03.READ_ONLY.mjs` plus `populated-history-target-linux-runner-caller-08/` caller/entry. This is a protocol refinement, not catch-and-ignore EROFS. Move genuine kernel proc observations to an external helper reading the still-live Node PID; retain in-process official Node/env/execArgv/loader/self-source checks. Three RO mounts, read-only root, no temporary writes and no SDK evaluation remain. Never derive kernel evidence from QEMU's guest-facing self files.

Root gives the new issued permit one freshly generated lower64 correlation nonce, consumed by one exact resolver invocation. Fixed argv is officialNode, fixedscript, exactnonce; logical Node argv must match, and external NUL kernel argv must equal QEMU, officialNode, fixedscript, same nonce. The nonce correlates this connected exec stream and PID; it is not ownership proof by itself. Caller output/permit/entry binds the exact new source and scope. No alternate script/nonce fallback. Source revisions require new exact permit schema review before issuance.

One Docker exec -i subprocess, no PTY. A bounded builtin-only Node program checks official runtime/source/env/loaders and emits READY once, then awaits START on its original stdin before any package-resolution/graph reads. READY has a closed prospective schema: kind, nonce, pid, node, logicalArgv, processEnv, embeddedLoaders, scriptSha256. Node object has exact version/platform/arch/path/sha256/execArgv/uid/euid/gid/egid; user999:999, no exec arguments. Parse unique keys/finite values and strictly bind the nonce/source/Node to the permit. PID strict canonical positive range, never Docker host PID or guessed PID from top order.

While that exact process waits, caller's separate fixed readonly Docker exec helpers obtain its /proc/<PID> stat-before, cmdline, full NUL environ, exe link, direct magic-exe hash and stat-after, plus finite sorted /proc inventory. External helper PID must differ from candidate. Read the candidate magic exe directly; guest-visible QEMU path may be absent. NUL records must terminate, environment keys unique and exact supplied3, no unsafe Node/loader vars. Parse stat using closing comm delimiter; both PIDs match candidate, same positive startTicks/PPID/live state. Require exact argv/nonce/Node/script, kernel QEMU9376/link and official Node89af separately. Exactly one matching candidate, no unexpected workload; finite helper processes only during their commands. Bound kernel tuple includes CID, candidatePID, startTicks, PPID, full argv/env bytes+hash, exe link/hash. Recheck brackets rather than trusting one sample or a process name.

Persist all actual helper argv/status/stdout/stderr, READY raw byte range and validated tuple/B3 before START. Caller sends one closed START frame {kind,nonce,pid,startTicks,attestationSha256} on original stdin only after every check and durable custody. Node rejects wrong/multiple/late frames. Node checks nonce/pid and strict token fields; actual kernel authority is caller evidence, not an opaque Node self-claim. Only then perform the unchanged builtin-only CJS4-root/metadata/1510-file verification. Still no SDK require/evaluation or SQL.

Node emits one RESULT frame with original root/metadata results, node proof and exact READY/START correlation, then remains live awaiting EXIT. While alive caller repeats the entire external proc bracket and validates the same CID/PID/startTicks/PPID/argv/env/exe tuple; a vanished/reused/re-execed PID cannot complete the proof. Raw before/after brackets and nonce/connected stream combine; none alone is sufficient. Persist RESULT and the second actual attestation; only then send one EXIT {kind,nonce,pid,startTicks,attestationSha256}. Node validates and exits0. Caller verifies raw protocol exactly2 LF JSON frames in READY→RESULT order, empty stderr, real child exit0 and all receipts. No parser filtering of warnings/extra stdout.

Use a fixed total900-second deadline for the whole one-use exec/rendezvous including readiness, attestation, graph/result and exit, existing helper bounds30 seconds and250ms interruption polling; protocol buffers bounded READY64KiB and RESULT2MiB, proc reads1MiB per file. Source tests must establish these bounds from actual selected output shape before activation. No renewed deadline or automatic retry. Node self-timeout/nonmatching input/EOF fails nonzero and never publishes success; raw error retained. Caller signal stops forward phases, preserves partial streams/ack bytes and performs only qualified owned-stop; exact sameCID final inspect must show stopped. Errors/unknown exit/excess output/inventory/process reuse/missing raw/stopped failure yields UNKNOWN and unresolved-owned-running quarantine where applicable. Restore handlers before terminal classification, retain additive late-interruption outcomes; outer entry must reconcile full original/returned/correction, not status alone.

A separate freshly owned keeper/birth/one-use authority is required for this reserve after the numeric diagnostic if consumed; never restart/reuse a diagnostic runner or consumed lease automatically. Initial PID1 inert proof and last one-process inventory, Node89af/loaders, source/permit rehash, empty directory full-parent proof and readonly controls all remain. Inspector independent pre-birth and post-output/cleanup scopes close before next work.

